KB-1b  the offset is BIGGER in the HTML bundle than in the raw SWF
--------------------------------------------------------------
Confirmed stage geometry: 700 x 400 px, 7:4, 30 fps (SWF header).
The first bundle builds stretched the player to width/height 100% --
a non-7:4 window made Ruffle letterbox internally, and the mouse to
stage transform across the letterbox is exactly where click offsets
live. On top of that, LibreWolf's privacy.resistFingerprinting
clamps devicePixelRatio to 1, its own known source of coordinate
drift on scaled displays.

Fixed in tools/build-singlefile.mjs: the player box now keeps the
stage's own 7:4 aspect ratio, so there is no internal letterbox to
mis-map through. Rebuild and replace the hosted copy. If a small
offset remains after that, it is KB-1 (the authentic 2006
center.hitTest behavior) and stays.

Quick differential test:
  1. raw .swf in desktop Ruffle        -> offset? = KB-1, original.
  2. bundle in stock Firefox/Chromium  -> gone? = it was the CSS.
  3. only in LibreWolf                 -> resistFingerprinting; try
     privacy.resistFingerprinting=false for the site.
